  "sanitized": true,
  "notes": "Trades read via REST (https://docs.polymarket.com/trading/manage-orders), modeled on the official SDK ClobTradeSchema in packages/bindings/src/clob/account.ts at reference commit 7fdbed42484b5d279c71aa36d3757d18968260da (raw source re-verified 2026-08-26). Unlike the websocket UserTradeEventSchema, EVERY ClobTradeSchema field is required (asset_id, bucket_index, fee_rate_bps, id, last_update, maker_address, maker_orders, market, match_time, outcome, owner, price, side, size, status, taker_order_id, trader_side, transaction_hash) and bucket_index is z.number(), not z.number().int(). REST maker orders follow the SDK MakerOrderSchema in the same file: asset_id, fee_rate_bps (nullable; the API serializes a missing maker fee rate as an empty string), maker_address, matched_amount, order_id, outcome, owner, price, side -- note there is no outcome_index on the REST maker order. Per the official SDK shared.ts, REST endpoints serialize the raw prefixed TRADE_STATUS_* constants (the user websocket channel serializes plain values), and 'MatchedNotBroadcasted currently appears only on trades read via REST, not on user stream trade events' -- hence TRADE_STATUS_MATCHED_NOT_BROADCASTED is modeled here in the REST layer only (conflict C-3 in docs/venue/verified-2026-08-24.md records the docs' contrary normalized-event claim). Owner fields are sanitized zero-UUID placeholders; ids, addresses, and transaction hashes are synthetic zero-values. Additional source: https://github.com/Polymarket/ts-sdk/blob/7fdbed42484b5d279c71aa36d3757d18968260da/packages/bindings/src/shared.ts",
